# MacroFit mobile — environment
#
# Copy to `mobile/.env` and fill in. Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` names are visible to the app.
#
# Restart the bundler after ANY change here: Expo inlines these values into the JS bundle
# at build time, so a running Metro keeps serving the old ones. Use `npx expo start --clear`.
#
# Everything below ships inside the bundle and is readable by anyone who has the APK.
# Never put a service-role key, or any other secret, in an EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable.
#
# `mobile/.gitignore` currently ignores only `.env*.local` — add `.env` to it before you
# commit, or name your file `.env.local`.

# --- Supabase (required) -----------------------------------------------------
# Project URL and anon/publishable key: Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
# The app throws on startup naming whichever of these is missing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- AI endpoints (required for chat, photo analysis and the coach) ----------
# Origin serving /api/chat, /api/analyze-photo and /api/recommend. Include the scheme;
# a trailing slash is stripped for you.
#
# MUST NOT be localhost. On a phone or emulator `localhost` and `127.0.0.1` resolve to the
# DEVICE ITSELF, not your dev machine, so every AI request fails with a connection error.
# This is the single most common setup mistake here. Use one of:
#
#   LAN IP of your dev machine   http://192.168.1.20:3000   (physical device or iOS sim)
#   Android emulator host alias  http://10.0.2.2:3000       (its name for your machine)
#   a deployed environment       https://your-app.vercel.app
#
# For a LAN IP: the phone must be on the same Wi-Fi, the dev server must bind 0.0.0.0
# rather than 127.0.0.1, and the firewall must allow the port. Find your IP with
# `ipconfig` (Windows) or `ifconfig | grep inet` (macOS/Linux).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3000

# --- USDA FoodData Central (recommended) -------------------------------------
# Free key, one minute to get: https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
#
# Omitting this falls back to the shared DEMO_KEY, which is capped at 30 requests a minute
# and 1000 a day PER IP ACROSS EVERY ANONYMOUS CALLER on the internet — not per app. In
# practice that means food search works at quiet times and fails at busy ones, with an
# error that reads like a connection problem.
#
# Worth knowing: this variable was documented here long before it was read. The shared
# search module took the key from `import.meta.env`, which Metro cannot evaluate, so on
# mobile it silently resolved to DEMO_KEY no matter what you set. Fixed; see
# src/core/utils/foodApiConfig.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USDA_API_KEY=DEMO_KEY

# --- Health Connect / Google Fit (Android) -----------------------------------
# Nothing to set. This section is here to say so, because it used to document an
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENABLE_HEALTH_CONNECT flag that no source file has ever read.
#
# The feature gates on capability instead: src/lib/healthConnect.ts checks Platform.OS,
# then getSdkStatus(), which reports whether THIS phone has the provider installed. A
# build-time flag could not answer that question, so there is nothing for one to decide.
#
# Note that Health Connect is the destination, not Google Fit. Fit displays a Health
# Connect record only if the user has turned on `Fit > Profile > Settings > Sync Fit with
# Health Connect`, which is off by default and which nothing in this app can change.

